    {
      "type": "security-audit",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T09:39:54Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
      "duration_ms": 65000,
      "summary": [
        "Reviewed 2 files (src/git/git-credentials.ts, src/tests/git-credentials.test.ts). 0 Critical, 0 High, 1 Medium (noted), 2 Low (noted). Security sign-off: PASS. All OWASP Top 10 categories reviewed. No blocking findings."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "security_issues": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
          "note": "OWASP A02 (Cryptographic Failures) — INFO: Tokens (PATs) are stored as plain strings in GitCredentialEntry.token and in config.json on disk. config.ts applies chmod 0o600 to config.json on POSIX (confirmed in src/config/config.ts:218), which is a solid defence-in-depth control. No additional encryption-at-rest is applied, which is consistent with the threat model for a local developer tool. No finding — observed and confirmed acceptable."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
          "note": "OWASP A03 (Injection) — PASS: injectCredentialToken() and injectCredentials() both inject the token via WHATWG URL property assignment (parsed.username = token), NOT string concatenation. The WHATWG URL serialiser percent-encodes all special characters (@, /, #, etc.) automatically. This is confirmed safe and tested by an explicit test case for adversarially crafted tokens containing '@' and '/'. No injection vector identified."
        },
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
          "note": "OWASP A01 (Broken Access Control) — Medium / Informational: resolveCredential() with an explicit credentialId performs only an exact id match (credentials.find(c => c.id === credentialId)). There is no URL-host cross-validation when an explicit ID is supplied — i.e. a caller could pass credentialId='github-personal' but url='https://evil.com/repo.git' and receive the GitHub credential. The token is then passed to injectCredentialToken() and embedded in the URL to be used in the git operation. Risk depends entirely on caller discipline: if the URL has already been validated against the configured host at the call site (e.g. in the orchestrators), this is safe. Since WP-002 is a utility layer, and callers are not yet implemented (WP-005 updates call sites), this is noted as a design concern for the Reviewer and future orchestrator implementors to validate that host/credential coherence is enforced at the call site."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
          "note": "OWASP A09 (Security Logging & Monitoring) — Low: stripEmbeddedCredentials() is already implemented and available to sanitise URLs before they appear in logs or error messages. Correct use of this utility at all git operation call sites is important to prevent token leakage in logs. This concern is for the orchestrators (WP-005 scope), not WP-002 itself. WP-002 provides the sanitisation primitive; ensuring it is applied is a call-site responsibility."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:40:59Z",
          "note": "OWASP A04/A07/A05/A06/A08/A10 — No issues identified. A04: No insecure defaults; null is returned for ambiguous or missing credential resolution. A07: No authentication/session logic in this module. A05: No configuration exposure. A06: No new third-party dependencies introduced — only Node.js built-in WHATWG URL API used. A08: No deserialization or build pipeline artefacts. A10: No server-side URL fetching; this module only manipulates URL strings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code-review",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T09:41:21Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T09:42:13Z",
      "duration_ms": 52000,
      "summary": [
        "Reviewed src/git/git-credentials.ts and src/tests/git-credentials.test.ts for WP-002.",
        "All four review dimensions (maintainability, best practices, performance, future context) pass with no blocking issues.",
        "No Fix-Forward changes applied — code is already clean. No behavioral changes made.",
        "Two Documentation-Forward items tagged for the Documentation agent.",
